{"number": 117, "text": "                                                                                                              ?\n\n             Exercises\n\n\n     55.1    Which phrasal verbs in the emails on the o   it\n             synonyms?  Write the phrasal verbs\n                                               next to their synonym.\n               continue\n\n                looks like\n                not complete\n\n                transmitted\n                be as good as\n                happen to\n                raising\n                look as if they are\n     55.2    Answer  these questions in full sentences using phrasal verbs.\n                Were you named  after anyone? If so, who were you named after?\n\n                Who, if anyone, do you take after in appearance?\n                Who, if anyone, do you take after in character?\n                Do you think that children should be treated as adults while they are growing up?\n                What reason might someone  have for dropping out of university?\n                Describe someone you know  who could pass for someone older than they really are.\n                Do you possess anything that has been handed down from your great-grandparents?\n                Do you think that both parents have an equally important role to play in bringing up their\n                children?\n                Until what age would you like to carry on working?\n             9\n\n      55.3    Complete this short biography using verbs from the opposite page.\n\n\n                 Richard Potts was born 100 years ago today in the same small town in Wales that he\n                 lives in now. He was (1)             after his maternal grandfather, Richard Jones,\n                 the distinguished sculptor, whom he was later said to (2)          after in both\n                 character and appearance. The young Richard was orphaned at an early age and was\n                 (3)                up by an aunt. He failed to (4)            up to his relatives’\n                 hopes for him by (5)               out of school at the age of 15. They were very\n                 concerned about what would (6)                of him and, although there must\n                 have been plenty of temptations encouraging the young boy to (7)            to\n                 gambling and drink, he resisted them all and (8)            up taking ajobina\n                 coal mine. He impressed the managers so much that he eventually (9)\n                 up as a member of the board. He (10)              on working until five years ago,\n                 when  ill health forced him to retire, but he is still a familiar figure around the streets of\n                 his home town.\n\n\n                 Over    to\n\n                 Read an obituary or article about the death of someone famous from any English language\n                 newspaper and note down any phrasal verbs that you find in it.\n\n\n                                                            English Phrasal Verbs in Use Intermediate 115", "char_count": 3032, "mean_conf": 92.82, "word_count": 386, "words": [{"text": "Exercises", "x0": 280, "y0": 72, "x1": 647, "y1": 145, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "55.1", "x0": 112, "y0": 295, "x1": 210, "y1": 343, "conf": 89, "bold": true}, {"text": "Which", "x0": 279, "y0": 291, "x1": 406, "y1": 330, "conf": 77, "bold": true}, {"text": "phrasal", "x0": 421, "y0": 292, "x1": 580, "y1": 337, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "verbs", "x0": 591, "y0": 298, "x1": 709, "y1": 337, "conf": 93, "bold": false}, {"text": "in", "x0": 722, "y0": 301, "x1": 760, "y1": 339, "conf": 93, "bold": false}, {"text": "the", "x0": 773, "y0": 305, "x1": 843, "y1": 343, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "emails", "x0": 856, "y0": 312, "x1": 995, "y1": 350, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "on", "x0": 1008, "y0": 325, "x1": 1059, "y1": 353, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "